---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Sourcing furniture from Indonesia"
  description="A buyer's guide to importing furniture from Indonesia: Jepara's furniture heritage, materials, how a container order works, and Indonesia versus Vietnam."
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Buyer guide" title="Sourcing furniture from Indonesia." lede="What to know before you import from Indonesia, and how it compares with Vietnam." />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="note">Draft for review by Evin before launch. Add specifics he can stand behind.</p>

      <h2>Why Jepara</h2>
      <p>Jepara, on the north coast of Central Java, is Indonesia's best known furniture town. Woodworking is the local trade, and skilled makers are close to where the wood is worked.</p>

      <h2>What you can source</h2>
      <p>Indonesian makers work in solid woods such as teak and mahogany, alongside veneers and mixed materials. Ask each supplier what species, grade and finish they use, and get it in writing.</p>

      <h2>How to import, in short</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Choose pieces and confirm the minimum order.</li>
        <li>Agree terms, usually FOB Indonesia.</li>
        <li>Check production and inspect before loading.</li>
        <li>Arrange freight and customs for your market.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>See <a href="/how-a-container-works">how a container works</a> with us.</p>

      <h2>Indonesia vs Vietnam</h2>
      <p>Both are established sources for furniture sold to the US. Vietnam is known for large factories and volume. Indonesia is known for solid wood and craft. The right choice depends on your range, quantities and timing, so compare actual quotes, lead times and inspection routines rather than countries.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand title="Talk to a maker in Jepara." text="Ask us about your range and your market." />
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 46rem; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: 1.9rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  .prose p, .prose li { margin-top: .8rem; color: var(--text-soft); }
  .prose ol { padding-left: 1.4rem; }
  .note { font-style: italic; }
</style>
